    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0fa5930e_db3ac066",
        "filename": "bluetooth/socket/aidl/android/hardware/bluetooth/socket/LeCocSpec.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 25,
      "author": {
        "id": 1884477
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-16T01:40:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You should mention the minimal value (23 for LE-U logical links).\nFrom the specification, the MTU is protocol specific. It might make more sense to let the application specify the value in full knowledge.\n\n(currently it seems to be fixed at the maximum value L2CAP_SDU_LENGTH_LE_MAX \u003d 0xffff)",
      "revId": "4ea5c12d3db34fbc25379f108f43db7f8c9aff80",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "dc0cd820_0211d4b2",
        "filename": "bluetooth/socket/aidl/android/hardware/bluetooth/socket/LeCocSpec.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 25,
      "author": {
        "id": 1959861
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-17T18:19:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Added document describing the specification and possible range. \nWhen offload stack/framework receives a packets, they allocate buffer and let offload app frees the buffer after picking up the packet. So, we need the configuration for stack.",
      "parentUuid": "0fa5930e_db3ac066",
      "revId": "4ea5c12d3db34fbc25379f108f43db7f8c9aff80",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "af548d9e_f561790a",
        "filename": "bluetooth/socket/aidl/android/hardware/bluetooth/socket/LeCocSpec.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 25,
      "author": {
        "id": 1884477
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-17T18:50:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What are the memory constraints on the MCU ?",
      "parentUuid": "dc0cd820_0211d4b2",
      "revId": "4ea5c12d3db34fbc25379f108f43db7f8c9aff80",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1d0321f1_326aee42",
        "filename": "bluetooth/socket/aidl/android/hardware/bluetooth/socket/LeCocSpec.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 25,
      "author": {
        "id": 1999105
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-18T00:57:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "MCU needs the RX MTU to be in the 1kB to 2kB range.",
      "parentUuid": "af548d9e_f561790a",
      "revId": "4ea5c12d3db34fbc25379f108f43db7f8c9aff80",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3cd7a14b_a56d17b1",
        "filename": "bluetooth/socket/aidl/android/hardware/bluetooth/socket/LeCocSpec.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 25,
      "author": {
        "id": 1884477
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-18T01:13:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ok, lets properly document that this value is the upper bound of the MTU that the offload stack can support internally. Letting the app negotiate the MTU might be a useful API addition still.",
      "parentUuid": "1d0321f1_326aee42",
      "revId": "4ea5c12d3db34fbc25379f108f43db7f8c9aff80",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "599449d6_595cecb7",
        "filename": "bluetooth/socket/aidl/android/hardware/bluetooth/socket/LeCocSpec.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 25,
      "author": {
        "id": 1959861
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-18T06:28:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In current flow, host stack has to know the required RX MTU to open the connection before talking to offload app. Do we want to add RX MTU option in regular socket as well? Then, host app can provide the RX MTU option through `BluetoothSocketSetting` when creating regular/offload sockets.",
      "parentUuid": "3cd7a14b_a56d17b1",
      "revId": "4ea5c12d3db34fbc25379f108f43db7f8c9aff80",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "84c60006_6e44c853",
        "filename": "bluetooth/socket/aidl/android/hardware/bluetooth/socket/LeCocSpec.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 30,
      "author": {
        "id": 1884477
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-16T01:40:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It absolutely makes sense to have it here.\nCan you please include the documentation from the specification:\n\n\u003e Specifies the maximum PDU payload size (in octets) that the\n\u003e offloaded Bluetooth stack is capable of receiving on this channel. L2CAP\n\u003e implementations shall support a minimum MPS of 23 octets and may support\n\u003e an MPS up to 65533 octets.",
      "revId": "4ea5c12d3db34fbc25379f108f43db7f8c9aff80",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f0a60fe1_a23bba79",
        "filename": "bluetooth/socket/aidl/android/hardware/bluetooth/socket/LeCocSpec.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 30,
      "author": {
        "id": 1959861
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-17T18:19:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For LE CoC, host stack is using MPS as LE ACL packet length. So, it seems we don\u0027t need to provide the configuration option. Removed MPS option.\n\n`uint16_t max_mps \u003d bluetooth::shim::GetController()-\u003eGetLeBufferSize().le_data_packet_length_;`",
      "parentUuid": "84c60006_6e44c853",
      "revId": "4ea5c12d3db34fbc25379f108f43db7f8c9aff80",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9eb0ed4e_a3a1b73d",
        "filename": "bluetooth/socket/aidl/android/hardware/bluetooth/socket/LeCocSpec.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 37,
      "author": {
        "id": 1884477
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-16T01:40:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Should the initial credit count be 0 regardless of what the offload stack wants ?\n\n1. The credit count might depend on the protocol the socket is opened for, in which case this configuration will not help when multiple protocols are supported.\n\n2. Having initial credit set to 0 ensures no packets is exchanged until the MCU gets hold of the socket.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 33,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 37,
        "endChar": 15
      },
      "revId": "4ea5c12d3db34fbc25379f108f43db7f8c9aff80",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e732b165_d59696c6",
        "filename": "bluetooth/socket/aidl/android/hardware/bluetooth/socket/LeCocSpec.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 37,
      "author": {
        "id": 1959861
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-17T18:19:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Updated description about specification. In spec, the value should be in range 0 to 65535. Credits must be set considering the buffer size to prevent the offload L2CAP layer receive buffer from overflowing. Setting credits per upper protocol can be complex to maintain while considering interoperability. The goal is to give enough credits to fit the memory at the beginning of the connection.",
      "parentUuid": "9eb0ed4e_a3a1b73d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 33,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 37,
        "endChar": 15
      },
      "revId": "4ea5c12d3db34fbc25379f108f43db7f8c9aff80",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7575876a_4f6dba9d",
        "filename": "bluetooth/socket/aidl/android/hardware/bluetooth/socket/LeCocSpec.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 37,
      "author": {
        "id": 1884477
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-17T18:50:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If you give 0 initial credits that won\u0027t happen, the remote device will not be able to send any data until the offload l2cap has released credits. \n\nAre you talking about the possibility of the offload l2cap overflowing from nanoapp PDUs ? That value will not be able to help since it represents initial rx credits only.",
      "parentUuid": "e732b165_d59696c6",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 33,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 37,
        "endChar": 15
      },
      "revId": "4ea5c12d3db34fbc25379f108f43db7f8c9aff80",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "14009ea1_c2325585",
        "filename": "bluetooth/socket/aidl/android/hardware/bluetooth/socket/LeCocSpec.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 37,
      "author": {
        "id": 1999105
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-18T00:57:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We want to set RX credits to a smaller value that (in combination with RX MTU) ensures that the remote device cannot exhaust the memory on the MCU.",
      "parentUuid": "7575876a_4f6dba9d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 33,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 37,
        "endChar": 15
      },
      "revId": "4ea5c12d3db34fbc25379f108f43db7f8c9aff80",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8bdf5e5c_adbb2378",
        "filename": "bluetooth/socket/aidl/android/hardware/bluetooth/socket/LeCocSpec.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 37,
      "author": {
        "id": 1884477
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-18T01:07:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is only the initial credits, once the connection is offloaded the MCU will have full control over the credit information. What I am suggesting is:\n\n- In the L2CAP_LE_CREDIT_BASED_CONNECTION_REQ frame the stack sets initial credits to 0 to ensure that no packets is transmitted until the MCU can handle them\n\n- Once the MCU receives the offloaded connection it can emit L2CAP_FLOW_CONTROL_CREDIT_IND to indicate the local buffers",
      "parentUuid": "14009ea1_c2325585",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 33,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 37,
        "endChar": 15
      },
      "revId": "4ea5c12d3db34fbc25379f108f43db7f8c9aff80",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "90742b53_d4e078fa",
        "filename": "bluetooth/socket/aidl/android/hardware/bluetooth/socket/LeCocSpec.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 37,
      "author": {
        "id": 1884477
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-18T01:09:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "To clarify again : this value does *not* indicate the number of RX buffers, the number can fluctuate and is indicate by the available credits shared with the remote device.",
      "parentUuid": "8bdf5e5c_adbb2378",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 33,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 37,
        "endChar": 15
      },
      "revId": "4ea5c12d3db34fbc25379f108f43db7f8c9aff80",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "89f31c50_ee0bd4b2",
        "filename": "bluetooth/socket/aidl/android/hardware/bluetooth/socket/LeCocSpec.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 37,
      "author": {
        "id": 1959861
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-18T06:28:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That\u0027s right. But if the host stack has already given too many RX credits like 65535, L2CAP_FLOW_CONTROL_CREDIT_IND will not be able to control RX traffic until all credits are used up because the credit value field in L2CAP_FLOW_CONTROL_CREDIT_IND represents number of credits the receiving device can\n*increment*.",
      "parentUuid": "90742b53_d4e078fa",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 33,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 37,
        "endChar": 15
      },
      "revId": "4ea5c12d3db34fbc25379f108f43db7f8c9aff80",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3ad64eaa_2b3471bc",
        "filename": "bluetooth/socket/aidl/android/hardware/bluetooth/socket/LeCocSpec.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 37,
      "author": {
        "id": 1884477
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-18T15:11:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e if the host stack has already given too many RX credits like 65535,\n\nWhy would the host stack give credit if the socket is offloaded ?",
      "parentUuid": "89f31c50_ee0bd4b2",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 33,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 37,
        "endChar": 15
      },
      "revId": "4ea5c12d3db34fbc25379f108f43db7f8c9aff80",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
